infographic hierarchy-tree-curved-line-rounded-rect-node
data
  root
    label Number N is a tuple of length N — every operation is tuple work
    children
      - label Add<A,B> — concatenate the two tuples
        desc Build both, spread into one, read ["length"] & number. Concatenation IS the type-level plus. Add<3,4> = 7.
      - label Subtract<A,B> — infer off the front
        desc Match BuildTuple<A> as [...BuildTuple<B>, ...infer Rest]; Rest["length"] is A − B. No prefix when A < B, so underflow falls to never.
      - label GreaterThan<A,B> — race the lengths
        desc Is B's tuple a prefix-superset of A's? Yes means A <= B (false); no means A > B (true). Equal lengths give false.
      - label ParseInt<S> — coerce a numeric string
        desc A template literal matches the digits; infer N extends number (TS 4.8+) coerces them back to a numeric literal type, pulling :42 out of a path.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
